  "title": "Counting on plain Pfaffian braces is #P-hard",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting 2-colourings of 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraphs whose incidence graphs are Pfaffian braces",
  "conclusion": "Weaving a hard source into a prism frame, with every crossing a ladder of plain cube junctions, gives plain Pfaffian braces (a bond lemma, a cube junction lemma and Hall's condition), so counting on plain Pfaffian braces is #P-hard. Among them planarity and the knot's atom, the Heawood graph, are the polynomial cases found.",
